{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm weighing whether to alias `double_underline` onto the existing underline2 bit, which is SGR 21 and already the ANSI double underline, or give it its own bit. The spec asks for a `double_underline` property and parsing for `double_underline`, `double-underline`, and `du`, and `uu` already maps to underline2, so I'm leaning toward reusing that bit and adding `du` as another alias.\n\nI'm looking at how to define `double_underline` as a second name for the bit already used by `underline2`, and I'm considering whether `Style(double_underline=True)` should also set `underline2`. The `__init__` and `_attributes` logic would need to OR the two parameters so either one sets bit 9. I still need to check the `_Bit` definition, `__add__`, `copy`, and the export code in `console.py`.\n\n","thinkingSignature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1oYWlrdS01LjUtMjAyNjEwMDd8Y2xhdWRlLW9uLWF3cyJ9"},{"type":"text","text":"The codebase already has a `underline2` attribute (SGR 21, the ANSI double-underline) in bit 9. Let me see the rest of `style.py` and the export code before deciding how to wire `double_underline` in."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Rc4Ukk8DtfpoPZ6ZxKhwee","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/app/rich/style.py","offset":600,"limit":160}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_019EmwR7FkT8Eb512wbE3zPF","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /app && sed -n 2370,2420p rich/console.py; grep -n \"class _Bit\" -A22 rich/style.py; grep -n \"underline2\\|uu\" tests/*.py | head -30; ls tests | head -80 | tr '\\n' ' '"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"openrouter","model":"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5","usage":{"input":2,"output":907,"cacheRead":12181,"cacheWrite":7398,"totalTokens":20488,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.00045349999999999996,"cacheRead":0.00012181,"cacheWrite":0.00092475,"total":0.00150026,"totalFromProvider":true},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reaso