{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":2,"output":8,"cacheRead":19579,"cacheWrite":4320,"totalTokens":23909,"cost":{"input":2.0000000000000002e-7,"output":0.000004,"cacheRead":0.00019579,"cacheWrite":0.00054,"total":0.00073999,"totalFromProvider":false},"cacheWrite1h":0},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"I'm settling on a design for a `double_underline` name that maps to bit 9, the SGR 21 attribute. It'll be a user-facing alias for the same attribute as underline2, so both names merge into one flag. I'm also planning to add a parser entry for it.\n\nI'm weighing whether to map the parser entry to the existing \"underline2\" key or to a new \"double_underline\" key. Mapping to \"double_underline\" and letting __init__ accept it keeps the parse output clearer, even though the bit is the same. I still need to work out how to merge the two None-valued arguments in __init__ without losing the unset state.\n\nSettling the merge of the two keyword arguments: if `double_underline` is set, it folds into `underline2`, keeping an unset value as unset and letting an explicit `False` stay off. Next I'm turning to the HTML output, where I'll add a `text-decoration: underline double` rule when the attribute is on.\n\nI'm settling the HTML side now: the rule goes in as `text-decoration: underline double`, matching the other HTML entries, while the SVG version keeps its trailing semicolon. I'm checking whether double should win over plain underline, and I'm keeping the existing pattern where strike also adds its own text-decoration rule.\n\nI'm leaving the `__rich_repr__` alone, since changing it could break the repr tests, and I'm checking that markup tags like `[double_underline]` and `[double-underline red]` will parse, since the tag regex accepts lowercase letters, hyphens, and underscores. The ANSI side should work as well, with bit 9 mapping to SGR code 21.\n\nNext I'm checking the docs for any mention of underline2 that would need a matching note for the new name, so I'll grep for it once the edits are in.\n\n"}}
